      "message": "Ifind this description a bit confusing. I think the intent is to explain why this is the safest order in which to apply the refs:\n\n- Patch-set ref before meta ref: the patch-set ref must exist before the change meta ref is updated to reference it.\n- Meta ref before branch: the change meta ref must exist before the branch is updated, so the commit pointed to by the branch is already associated with a valid, reachable change.\n\nSomething like:\n\n```\n// Apply refs in dependency order:\n// 1. Patch-set refs, so the referenced patch-set objects exist.\n// 2. Change meta refs, so the change is valid and navigable.\n// 3. All other refs, such as branches and tags, which may point to those commits.\n```",
